       ported features of the sockets API for UNIX domain sockets on Linux.

       UNIX domain sockets do not support the transmission of out‐of‐band data
       (the MMSSGG__OOOOBB flag for sseenndd(2) and rreeccvv(2)).

       The sseenndd(2) MMSSGG__MMOORREE flag is not supported by UNIX domain sockets.

       Before Linux 3.4, the use of MMSSGG__TTRRUUNNCC in the _f_l_a_g_s argument of rreeccvv(2)
       was not supported by UNIX domain sockets.

